    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Drug-susceptible pulmonary tuberculosis, treatment completed (A15.0)</content>. Treatment completed, with culture conversion and a full clinical response. The chest X-ray today shows the cavity closed, with residual scarring in the right upper lobe. End-of-treatment ALT 30, AST 28, bilirubin 0.6, and hemoglobin 14.4, all normal. Dr. Navarro reviewed the results by message today and advises no routine follow-up after treatment. [S]<list><item>No further tuberculosis medicine.</item><item>Return the same day for cough lasting more than two weeks, fever, night sweats, or weight loss, which could mean relapse.</item><item>Keep today&apos;s chest X-ray as the baseline for any future comparison.</item><item>Health department notified that treatment is complete.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol use disorder, mild, improving (F10.10)</content>. Low-risk drinking since the spring. AUDIT-C 3, PHQ-9 3. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide. [S]<list><item>Continue monthly counseling.</item><item>Keep to no more than two drinks on any day.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Symptom review: cough, sputum, hemoptysis, fever, night sweats</td><td>At least monthly during treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight</td><td>At least monthly during treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>65.5 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Hepatitis symptom review (nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, jaundice, dark urine)</td><td>Every visit and every observed dose</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None reported at any observed dose</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Liver tests (ALT, AST, bilirubin)</td><td>Baseline, at two weeks, then monthly because of alcohol use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>ALT 30, AST 28 U/L, bilirubin 0.6 mg/dL, all normal at the end of treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Liver tests after the sick visit and in months four and five</td><td>Two weeks after the sick visit, then monthly</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Not drawn: no visit was scheduled between the sick visit and the end of treatment, and no standing order was placed. He reported no hepatitis symptoms on daily video calls, and the end-of-treatment tests are normal, so no harm is evident. Corrective action: standing monthly liver-test orders at the start of treatment for every patient with a risk factor</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Hemoglobin</td><td>At the end of treatment when low at baseline</td><td>Completed today</td><td>14.4 g/dL, up from 12.6 at diagnosis</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Sputum AFB smear and culture</td><td>Monthly until two consecutive cultures are negative</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Two consecutive negative cultures (third week and two months); no further sputum needed</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Two-month sputum culture</td><td>At the end of the intensive phase; decides the continuation length in cavitary disease</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No growth; continuation phase kept at four months</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Chest X-ray</td><td>At diagnosis; at two months only if the first cultures were negative; at the end of treatment as a new baseline</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Cavity closed; residual right upper lobe scarring</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Doses observed and missed (video-observed therapy)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>All 182 doses observed</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Peripheral neuropathy check, with pyridoxine</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No neuropathy; pyridoxine stopped with isoniazid</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Notification of treatment completion to the health department</td><td>At the end of treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Sent today</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Alcohol use (AUDIT-C for the past month)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 3 for the past month</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Brief counseling about alcohol and liver risk</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Low-risk limits agreed now that treatment is over</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Counseling with a substance-use counselor</td><td>Every one to two weeks during treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Monthly</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression screen (PHQ-9)</td><td>At diagnosis and at the end of treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 3, item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide-risk review and safety plan, with the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No thoughts of suicide</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Infectious diseases review</td><td>At two months and at the end of treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dr. Navarro reviewed the end-of-treatment results by message; no routine follow-up</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Complete 182 doses of treatment under video-observed therapy within six months. Outcome by 1873-08-18: All 182 doses completed: 56 in the intensive phase and 126 in the continuation phase, with one dose held during a stomach illness and made up at the end [S]</item><item>Sputum culture negative at two months. Outcome by 1873-08-18: Two-month culture showed no growth, so the continuation phase stayed at four months [S]</item><item>No alcohol during treatment, to protect his liver. Outcome by 1873-08-18: Not fully met: no drinking for most of the six months, with one evening of heavy drinking at a party about three months into treatment; AUDIT-C 3 at the end [S]</item><item>Return to work once he is no longer infectious. Outcome by 1873-03-17: Released from home isolation after three negative sputum smears and back at work four weeks into treatment [S]</item><item>Weight back to at least 64 kg by the end of treatment. Outcome by 1873-08-18: 65.5 kg at the end of treatment, from 58.0 kg at diagnosis [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Official American Thoracic Society/Centers for Disease Control and Prevention/Infectious Diseases Society of America Clinical Practice Guidelines: Treatment of Drug-Susceptible Tuberculosis (2016); An official ATS statement: hepatotoxicity of antituberculosis therapy (2006); Guidelines for the investigation of contacts of persons with infectious tuberculosis: recommendations from the National Tuberculosis Controllers Association and CDC (2005); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Substance Use Disorders (2021); Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Adult preventive visit in about a month. Same-day visit for symptoms of relapse. Next scheduled visit 1873-09-22: adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

